  (text "CONNECTORS (field side, GND_ISO domain).  Both connectors are wired in parallel on the same nets - use ONE at a time.\nDB9 (J5, male, DTE pinout, right-angle):  pin 2 = RS-232 RXD (input)   pin 3 = RS-232 TXD (output)   pin 5 = GND_ISO   pin 7 = RS-232 RTS (output)   pin 8 = RS-232 CTS (input)\n                                           pin 1 = RS-485 B   pin 6 = RS-485 A   (RS-485 in/out, half-duplex)   pins 4 (DTR) and 9 (RI) = not connected\n5-pos pluggable terminal (J6, 5.08 mm):  1 = GND_ISO   2 = RS-232 TXD (out)   3 = RS-232 RXD (in)   4 = RS-485 A   5 = RS-485 B     (RTS/CTS are DB9 only)\nProtection: RS-232 lines each have a bidirectional 15 V TVS (SMAJ15CA, D10-D13) to GND_ISO (RS-232 swings +/-12 V so SM712 would clip).  RS-485 A/B: SM712-class array (D14, -7/+12 V common-mode window) to GND_ISO, placed after the 10 R series resistors on the Serial sheet.\nA/B naming follows the SN65HVD72 datasheet (A = non-inverting side idles high with bias fitted); some vendors label the pair the other way round.  MODE select (RS-232 vs RS-485) is on the Isolation + Serial sheet (GP5 MODE_SEL / JP4).\nDB9 shell / mounting holes are not connected in the schematic (tie to GND_ISO or chassis in layout)."
    (at 20 30 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "c48874d8-06c5-40aa-8ea3-23c925f949a9")
  )
